<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ʻŌlelo Hawaiʻi (Hawaiian) overlay — issue #210.

    Statutory context:
      * ʻŌlelo Hawaiʻi is a co-official language of the State of Hawaiʻi
        under Article XV, Section 4 of the State Constitution
        (1978 amendment): "English and Hawaiian shall be the official
        languages of Hawaiʻi…"
      * The 1896 Act 57 banning Hawaiian-language instruction was repealed
        in 1986; the ʻAha Pūnana Leo and Hawaiian-medium schools have
        rebuilt the speaker base. Software shipping to Hawaiʻi has an
        affirmative obligation to support the language.

    Honest scope statement:
      This PR ships only the language-selector UI strings. They use
      orthography from the Pukui–Elbert *Hawaiian Dictionary* with ʻokina
      (glottal stop) and kahakō (long-vowel macron: ā ē ī ō ū) applied
      correctly. The clinical pattern explanations are NOT translated in
      this PR — translating sepsis criteria, NEWS2, AHI, ECG indications,
      and mg/dL ↔ mmol/L thresholds into ʻōlelo Hawaiʻi without a fluent
      reviewer who is also clinically trained would produce dangerously
      register-mismatched text. Empty keys would shadow the English
      default; absent keys fall back to English instead.

      Future PR: commission Hawaiʻi-based clinical translators (ʻAha
      Pūnana Leo network; Papa Ola Lōkahi for Native Hawaiian health
      terminology) before translating pattern explanations.

    ʻOkina (ʻ) and kahakō policy:
      * ʻokina is the glottal-stop letter U+02BB (modifier letter turned
        comma), not a straight apostrophe. Render in source as ʻ.
      * kahakō are the standard combining macrons (ā ē ī ō ū).
      * Examples used here: ʻōlelo, Hawaiʻi.

    DO NOT machine-translate pattern_*_explanation / _suggested_action
    keys into this file. Empty is correct.
-->
<resources>

    <!-- == Settings UI strings (language selector) == -->
    <string name="settings_language_title">ʻŌlelo</string>
    <string name="settings_language_subtitle">E hoʻololi i ka ʻōlelo o ka ʻōnaehana no nā kikokikona o Bios. Pili kēia i nā leka makaʻala a me nā ʻōlelo o ka pakuhi. E hoʻokumu hou iā Bios ma hope o ka hoʻololi.</string>
    <string name="settings_language_system_default">Hoʻonohonoho mau o ka ʻōnaehana</string>
    <string name="settings_language_apply">E hoʻohana</string>
</resources>
